A||N||3||Rumor||Squeaky Belt on an 85 GT (V6)||||1||
Z||000000||Rumor||12-27-2001||03:25 AM||||All,<P>  My belt squeals on startup when it is cold outside, and if I turn on the heater during the first five minutes or so. If I rev the engine to 2,500-3,000 for one or two seconds, it usually goes away, but I usually just let the engine warm up, and then it behaves. Is this normal (I have seen others mention the squeal on the forum), is this going to wear out the belt, and is there anything I can do to hush this lil' piggy?<BR>As always, THANKS for all your help - you've helped out this Fiero-newbie more times then I can count theses last two months!<P>-Rumor<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||tesmith66||12-27-2001||07:56 AM||||Check the alternator bracket. They have a nasty habit of cracking. I don't know if GM still makes them, but if so, they are not too expensive. I got mine (4 years ago) for $25 at a dealer. Someone was selling welded up steel ones on the net a few years ago, but I can't find those anymore. Maybe someone else knows.<P>------------------<BR>Timothy E. Smith<BR>1986 SE V6<BR>1984 Coupe||||reg||1
